# the argument of augustine-1.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# Augustine argues that leaving God is a matter of disordered affections, not of place.
# S1-S3 are lament and prayer, and S6 (the prodigal son) is an illustration: none is a premise.
atom	affections_remove	darkened affections is removal from God
atom	place_removes	men leave God or return unto Him by their feet, or change of place
atom	lustful_is_darkened	lustful affections are darkened affections
atom	distance_in_affections	the true distance from God's face is in lustful, that is, darkened affections
P1	S4	affections_remove
P2	S5	¬place_removes	kind conceptual
P3	S7	lustful_is_darkened	kind conceptual
# The text never states this link; the "So then" of S7 relies on it.
A1	-	affections_remove ∧ ¬place_removes → distance_in_affections
C	S7	distance_in_affections	from P1 P2 A1
